        <obo:IAO_0000115>Lower, narrow portion of the uterus where it joins with the top end of the vagina.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>The narrow caudal end of the uterus that opens into the vagina. [TFD][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>The evolution of mammals is associated with radical changes in their reproductive biology, particularly the structure and function of the female reproductive organs. These changes include the evolution of the uterus, cervix, vagina, placenta and specialized cell types associated with each of those structures.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000007>cervical</obo:UBPROP_0000007>
