        <owl:annotatedTarget>In the anatomy of animals, an avian pallium is the dorsal telencephalon of a bird&apos;s brain. Pallium of avian species tend to be relatively large, comprising ~75% of the telencephalic volume.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:source>Wikipedia:Avian_pallium</oboInOwl:source>
        <oboInOwl:taxon>NCBITaxon:8782</oboInOwl:taxon>
