        <owl:annotatedTarget>A complex network of conduits that begins with the canals of Hering (intralobar bile duct) and progressively merges into a system of interlobular, septal, and major ducts which then coalesce to form the extrahepatic bile ducts, which finally deliver bile to the intestine, and in some species to the gallbladder.</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>DOI:10.1002/ar.20664</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    </owl:Axiom>
