        <obo:IAO_0000115>Acellular structure composed of calcium carbonate located in the otolith organ.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>Currently represented as part of the otolith membrane, but they may also be considered to be embedded in this membrane</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Portion of organism substance composed of calcium carbonate located in the otolith organ.[TAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000002>relationship loss: develops_from immature otolith (TAO:0000139)[TAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000002>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000007>otoconial</obo:UBPROP_0000007>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000007>otolithic</obo:UBPROP_0000007>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>Mammals have many tiny otoconia and fish have three large otoliths[ZFIN:df]</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
