        <owl:annotatedTarget>The organizer is a central feature of vertebrate embryogenesis. It was first characterized in functional terms in amphibians by Spemann and Mangold (1924), and homologous tissues have since been identified in representatives of most other vertebrate classes, including mammals (the node), birds (Henson&apos;s node) and teleost fish (the embryonic shield).[well established][VHOG]</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:date_retrieved>2012-09-17</oboInOwl:date_retrieved>
        <oboInOwl:external_class>VHOG:0000598</oboInOwl:external_class>
