                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002162"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCBITaxon_33213"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A structure directly adjacent to the outer surface of the plasma membrane of an ovum. It is composed mostly of protein fibers, with protein receptors needed for sperm binding, binding to sperm plasma membrane receptors. The species-specificity between these receptors contributes to prevention of breeding between different species [Wikipedia]. A protective layer around the egg[FBbt].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>TODO - consider GO CC request. GO:0030704-vitelline membrane formation considered a subclass of CC organization</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Thin membrane enclosing and immediately adjacent to the ovum. Produced in the ovary.[AAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000002>relationship loss: part_of zygote (AAO:0010324)[AAO]</obo:UBPROP_0000002>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>Outside the plasma membrane, three envelopes surround the ovum. The first, the primary egg envelope, lies between the plasma membrane and the surrounding cells of the ovary. The most consistent component of this primary layer is the vitelline membrane, a transparent jacket of fibrous protein. In mammals, the homologous structure is called the zona pellucida.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>zona pellucida - vitelline membrane</oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>AAO:0010332</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>BTO:0001450</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FBbt:00000042</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>GAID:1318</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MESH:D014817</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Vitelline_membrane</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>XAO:0000030</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>m. vitellina</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>yolk sac membrane</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>zona pellucida</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0003125</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#dubious_grouping"/>
        <rdfs:label>vitelline membrane</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
