        <obo:IAO_0000115>A meninx that is part of a brain [Automatically generated definition].</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000001>Meninges that are part of the brain. [Bgee_curator][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000001>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>In fishes, the meninges consist of a single membrane, the primitive meninx, wrapped around the brain and spinal cord. With the adoption of terrestrial life, the meninges doubled. In amphibians, reptiles, and birds, the meninges include a thick outer dura mater derived from mesoderm and a thin inner secondary meninx. (...) In mammals, the dura mater persists, but division of the secondary meninx yields both the arachnoid and the pia mater from ectomesoderm.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>CALOHA:TS-2147</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:32662</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0000813</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:180949007</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VHOG:0000013</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>brain meninges</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>meninges of brain</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>meninx of brain</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0003547</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#organ_slim"/>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#pheno_slim"/>
        <rdfs:label>brain meninx</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Axiom>
        <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0003547"/>
        <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
