        <owl:annotatedTarget>Intermediate phalanges are bones found in the limbs of most vertebrates. In humans, they are the bones of the finger and toe which lie in the middle, between the two wrinkly joints. The thumb and big toe do not have intermediate phalanges. In most other vertebrates, they have a corresponding place in their limbs, whether they be paw, wing, hoof or fin</owl:annotatedTarget>
        <oboInOwl:source>WP</oboInOwl:source>
    </owl:Axiom>
