    <!-- http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004772 -->

    <owl:Class rdf:about="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0004772">
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0000094"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:nodeID="genid25199"/>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051"/>
                <owl:someValuesFrom rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_18085"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The tarsi (tarsal plates) are two comparatively thick, elongated plates of dense connective tissue, about 2.5 cm. in length; one is found in each eyelid, and contributes to its form and support. They directly abut the lid margins.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000008>In most taxa (birds, mammals, lizards), the tarsal plate is described as a dense, fibrous connective tissue, possibly including cartilage, present within one or both of the upper and lower eyelids (Gau- thier et al., 1988; Rieppel, 2000). In humans, the tarsal plate of the upper eyelid is composed of collagens types I, III, and V, as well as glycosaminogly- cans (chondroitin sulphate 4 and 6), aggrecan, and cartilage oligomeric matrix proteins but lacks collagen type II as well as chondrocytes (Milz et al., 2005). Thus, for humans, the upper tarsal plate represents neither a truly fibrous nor a truly cartilagi- nous element but instead one that is composed of a unique transitional tissue (Milz et al., 2005). In many birds, lizards, and Sphenodon (the tuatara), the upper eyelid has lim- ited mobility and a putative tarsal plate is instead found within the lower eyelid (Underwood, 1970; Gau- thier et al., 1988).</obo:UBPROP_0000008>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:59086</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0000270</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C33736</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:362529005</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C0459586</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Tarsus_(eyelids)</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>tarsal plate</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>tarsal plate of eyelid</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>tarsus palpebralis</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>eyelid tarsi</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>tarsi</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0004772</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#organ_slim"/>
        <rdfs:label>eyelid tarsus</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
    <owl:Restriction rdf:nodeID="genid25199">
