            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>In anatomy, the common hepatic artery is a short blood vessel that supplies oxygenated blood to the liver, pylorus (a part of the stomach), duodenum (a part of the small intestine), pancreas, and gall bladder. It arises from the celiac artery and has the following branches: the hepatic artery proper, the gastroduodenal artery and the right gastric artery.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0000308</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA:8570</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:37206</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:14771</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MA:0003094</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>SCTID:244263001</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Common_hepatic_artery</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>galen:CommonHepaticArtery</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>arteria hepatica communis</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>common hepatic</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0005436</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#human_reference_atlas"/>
