        <obo:IAO_0000115>Mesenchyme that is part of a pharyngeal arch 2.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>In all vertebrates, the pharyngeal apparatus develops from a series of bulges found on the lateral surface of the head, the pharyngeal arches, which consist of a number of different embryonic cell types. Each arch has an external covering of ectoderm and inner covering of endoderm, and between these a mesenchymal filling of neural crest with a central core of mesoderm.[well established][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0000066</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA:625</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:16279</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:295698</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VHOG:0001102</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>2nd pharyngeal arch mesenchyme</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>2nd branchial arch mesenchyme</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>pharyngeal arch 2 mesenchyme</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0005689</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>2nd arch mesenchyme</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
