                <owl:onClass rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/UBERON_0001436"/>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The interphalangeal articulations of hand are hinge-joints of the phalanges of the hand. There are two sets (except in the thumb): &apos;proximal interphalangeal joints&apos; (PIP), those between the first (also called proximal) and second (intermediate) phalanges &apos;distal interphalangeal joints&apos; (DIP), those between the second and third (distal) phalanges A similar group of articulations also function in the toes.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:IAO_0000116>consider renaming: &apos;finger&apos; is ambiguous as the term in some usages excludes the thumb (we include it)</obo:IAO_0000116>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:36336</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>FMA:35285</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>MESH:D005384</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
