        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>A mesentery that is part of a foregut-midgut junction.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <obo:UBPROP_0000003>Although all vertebrates have a digestive tract and accessory glands, various parts of this system are not necessarily homologous, analogous, or even present in all species. Therefore, broad comparisons can be best made under the listings of headgut, foregut, midgut, pancreas and biliary system, hindgut.[uncertain][VHOG]</obo:UBPROP_0000003>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EHDAA2:0000575</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>EMAPA:16365</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>VHOG:0000430</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>foregut-midgut junction mesentery</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0009483</oboInOwl:id>
        <oboInOwl:inSubset rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/uberon/core#emapa_ehdaa2"/>
        <rdfs:label>mesentery of foregut-midgut junction</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
