            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <obo:IAO_0000115>The tracheoesophageal septum is formed from the tracheoesophageal folds which fuse in the midline to form a structure called tracheoesophageal septum. It divides the esophagus from the trachea. It divides the foregut tube into the laryngotracheal tube ventrally and esophagus dorsally. Developmental abnormalities can lead to a tracheoesophageal fistula.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C34316</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>Wikipedia:Tracheoesophageal_septum</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
        <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>esophagotracheal septum</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>tracheoesophageal ridges</oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym>
        <oboInOwl:id>UBERON:0036070</oboInOwl:id>
        <rdfs:label>tracheoesophageal septum</rdfs:label>
    </owl:Class>
